{"id":"65e1c4e5-602d-4558-8dd8-ca40acf49c0a","lean_formalization_count":0,"has_bounty":false,"number":339406,"title":"Author's conjecture on improving a modified Bessel-function integral inequality","statement":"Let $n<1$, let $\nu\\geq 1-n+\\sqrt{2(1-n)}$, and define\n\n$$\n\\alpha_{\\nu,n}:=\\nu+n-\\sqrt{(\\nu+n)^2-2\\nu-1}.\n$$\n\nFor the modified Bessel function of the second kind $K_\\mu$, the author conjectures that, for every $x>0$,\n\n$$\n\\int_x^\\infty\\frac{K_{\\nu+n}(t)}{t^\\nu}\\\\,\\mathrm{d}t>\\frac{K_{\\nu+n-\\alpha_{\\nu,n}}(x)}{x^\\nu}.\n$$\n\nThe exponent shift is claimed to be best possible up to the symmetry $K_{-\\mu}(x)=K_\\mu(x)$: defining\n\n$$\n\\alpha'_{\\nu,n}:=\\nu+n+\\sqrt{(\\nu+n)^2-2\\nu-1},\n$$\n\nany $\\beta\\notin\\\\{\\alpha_{\\nu,n},\\alpha'_{\\nu,n}\\\\}$ either gives a strictly smaller right-hand side for every $x>0$, or fails to provide a lower bound at some $y>0$. The source also records equality in the corresponding inequality when $n=1$, for all $\\nu\\in\\mathbb{R}$; the conjectured statement itself is presented under $n<1$.","post_type":"conjecture","status":"open","tags":["bessel-functions","integral-inequalities","special-functions"],"collections":[],"author":null,"is_author":false,"importance":"corpus","first_stated_year":2018,"first_stated_year_source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.00524","documented_by_year":null,"documented_by_source_url":null,"references":"Source: https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.00524\n\nStatus: no resolution is reported in the source (as of June 2018).","source_name":"Robert E. Gaunt, “Inequalities for some integrals involving modified Bessel functions”, arXiv:1806.00524 (2018).","source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.00524","progress":null,"vote_count":0,"my_vote":null,"bookmarked":false,"bookmark_count":0,"subscribed":false,"view_count":15,"created_at":"2026-08-11T05:40:24.850249Z","edited_at":null,"moderator_edited_at":null,"comments":[],"attachments":[],"solutions":[],"model_attempts":[],"human